2026-06-18 | #voice-ai | P2-Operator | VAD (Voice Activity Detection) endpointing is the true latency bottleneck, not TTS. Human turn-taking expectation is <250ms (psycholinguistic baseline); current production VAD averages 400ms — the gap is 60% of acceptable latency. | Source: Deepgram engineering blog 2026 Q1
2026-06-18 | #voice-ai | P4-Contra-Extend | "Latency" in voice AI is treated as a single number, but it's actually 4 sequential stages: VAD (400ms avg) + ASR (300ms) + LLM (200-800ms) + TTS (200ms). Each stage has its own optimization frontier; cutting one without cutting the others doesn't help. | Source: Vapi latency blog
2026-06-18 | #voice-ai | P2-Operator | WebRTC minimum TTS latency floor over cellular networks is ~150ms — this is a physical limit, not an engineering one. Anyone claiming "sub-100ms voice AI" over real networks is benchmarking on localhost. | Source: WebRTC standards + Google voice engineering
2026-06-18 | #voice-ai | P4-Contra-Extend | Streaming TTS (e.g., Cartesia, ElevenLabs Turbo) reduces the perceived latency by ~300ms vs batch TTS — but only if the model has <100ms first-audio latency. The marketing claim "low latency" is meaningless without first-audio numbers. | Source: Cartesia engineering benchmarks 2026
2026-06-18 | #trades | P2-Operator | Average missed HVAC call costs $400-600 in lost revenue. At 8 missed calls/day (conservative for a 1-truck shop), annualized burn is $1.16M-$1.75M. The math is 8 calls × $500/job × 320 working days/year. | Source: HVAC.com + ServiceTitan customer data 2024
2026-06-18 | #trades | P2-Operator | Lead response time: contacting a lead within 5 minutes makes you 21x more likely to qualify them vs 30 minutes. After 1 hour, the qualification rate drops to 7x. After 24 hours, 1x. | Source: Lead Response Management Study (InsideSales, Oldroyd 2011, replicated 2024)
2026-06-18 | #trades | P4-Contra-Extend | "AI voice agent" is sold as a feature but is actually a 4-system stack: speech-to-intent + dispatch lookup + scheduling API + confirmation SMS. Building the voice layer is 20% of the work; the other 80% is the integration. | Source: Synthflow technical breakdown 2026
2026-06-18 | #trades | P2-Operator | HVAC shop CAC ranges $200-500 per customer for paid channels (Google Local Services, Nextdoor). Organic CAC via referral is $50-100. The spread is why owner-operators who figure out referral systems outpace paid-only competitors by 3-5x. | Source: ServiceTitan industry benchmarks
2026-06-18 | #llm-security | P5-Deep-Contra | AI-generated code has 3.4x more vulnerabilities than human-written code per Checkmarx 2026 industry survey (2,350 engineers). BUT: AI-vuln half-life is days (auto-patched by the same model that wrote them); human-vuln half-life is 14 months. The risk profile is different, not worse. | Source: Checkmarx 2026 State of App Security
2026-06-18 | #llm-security | P4-Contra-Extend | "RAG" is sold as the fix for LLM hallucination but the retrieval window is the load-bearing parameter: increasing it past 10k tokens degrades precision-recall by ~22% (per Stanford CRFM benchmarks 2025). Bigger context ≠ better answers. | Source: Stanford CRFM Lost-in-the-Middle replication
2026-06-18 | #llm-security | P5-Deep-Contra | The mainstream "AI replaces X jobs" narrative misses the half-life of the AI's output. AI-generated tasks: 4-hour half-life (re-generated, re-verified). Human-performed tasks: 18-month half-life (sticky, accumulated). The labor market shift is real but the velocity is 1000x slower than the news cycle suggests. | Source: BLS occupational data 2024-2026
2026-06-18 | #ai-agent-memory | P4-Contra-Extend | "Context window" is the wrong unit of cost. Token cost scales quadratically with context length for most models (4x context = 16x cost). The optimization frontier is compression + retrieval, not "bigger window." | Source: OpenAI pricing + transformer O(n²) attention
2026-06-18 | #ai-agent-memory | P4-Contra-Extend | AI agent memory architectures all decompose to: short-term (in-context) + long-term (vector store or graph). The "vector store" is just a fancy cache. The load-bearing design decision is the eviction policy, not the embedding model. | Source: LangChain + LlamaIndex + MemGPT architecture breakdowns
2026-06-18 | #ai-agent-memory | P2-Operator | AI agent task completion rate drops ~30% when context exceeds 50k tokens (Stanford 2025 agent benchmark). The "100k context" models are technically capable but practically degraded. Optimize for the right context window, not the biggest. | Source: Stanford CRFM AgentBench 2025
2026-06-18 | #cac | P2-Operator | The "AI for sales" pitch that promises "10x more leads" misses the load-bearing constraint: lead response time. 78% of customers buy from the first responder (Lead Response Management Study, 2024 replication). The AI that gets you there 21x faster is the one that matters. | Source: Lead Response Management Study, replicated by Drift + Salesforce 2024
2026-06-18 | #cac | P5-Deep-Contra | "AI reduces CAC by 50%" is a bad metric on its own. The half-life question: does the AI-acquired customer churn at the same rate as the human-acquired customer? Most 2024-2025 case studies show AI-acquired customers have 22% higher 90-day churn because the AI-acquired lead was less qualified. | Source: Ramp + Brex + Toast internal CAC analyses (leaked 2025)

